  <h2 id="trial">The free trial</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Starts automatically the first time Ravenburst opens with an internet connection. No account, no card.</li>
    <li>Lasts <strong>7 days</strong> on that computer. Every feature is available.</li>
    <li>A bar at the top of the window shows the days left, with <strong>Enter License Code</strong> and <strong>Buy Now</strong> buttons.</li>
    <li>A trial belongs to the computer, so reinstalling Ravenburst doesn't start a new one.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="after-trial">When the trial ends</h2>
  <p>You keep your work and can keep writing. <strong>Writing, editing, saving, opening projects and File → Print all keep working.</strong> These need a license:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Compile / Export, including the Print format in the Compile dialog</li>
    <li>Git Backup</li>
    <li>Cloud Storage (Google Drive)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Everything you write is in your own project file on your own computer, licensed or not. See <a href="/docs/data-privacy">Your Files &amp; Privacy</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="activate">Activating</h2>
  <p>When you buy Ravenburst you receive an activation code by email. It starts with <code>RAVENBURST-</code> and is tied to the email address you bought with.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Choose <span class="menu">Help → Enter Activation Code…</span>, or click <strong>Enter License Code</strong> in the trial bar.</li>
    <li>Enter the <strong>email address</strong> you bought with.</li>
    <li>Paste the <strong>activation code</strong>.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Activate</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Activation registers the computer as one of your devices, so connect to the internet if you can. If you can't, the code is still checked and accepted on the computer itself, and the device is registered the next time Ravenburst checks in.</p>
  <p>After three wrong attempts in a row, the dialog waits five minutes before letting you try again.</p>

  <h2 id="devices">Your devices</h2>
  <p>One license covers <strong>up to 3 computers</strong>. To move it to a new computer, free up a slot on the old one first:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>On the old computer, choose <span class="menu">Help → Deactivate License on This Device</span> and confirm.</li>
    <li>On the new computer, enter your email and code as above.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Ravenburst recognises a computer from details such as its name and hardware. Renaming the computer or replacing major parts can make it look like a new device. If that uses up your slots, email us and we'll reset them.</p>

  <h2 id="offline">Working offline</h2>
  <p>Once activated, Ravenburst works without the internet. About every 30 days it quietly checks in to confirm the license is still valid. If you're offline, nothing happens: the check simply waits until next time.</p>
  <p>If a license is cancelled (for example after a refund), the next check-in shows a banner, and export, Git Backup and Cloud Storage stop working three days later. If you see that banner and think it's a mistake, email <a href="mailto:support@ravenburst.com">support@ravenburst.com</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="status">Checking your license</h2>
  <p><span class="menu">Help → License Status</span> opens <span class="menu">Preferences → License</span>, which shows whether you're licensed or on a trial (and how many days are left), the email the license belongs to, and the versions it covers.</p>

  <h2 id="problems">Problems</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Lost your code?</strong> Email <a href="mailto:support@ravenburst.com">support@ravenburst.com</a> from the address you bought with and we'll send it again.</li>
    <li><strong>“Already activated on 3 devices”</strong>: deactivate an old computer, or email us if you no longer have it.</li>
    <li><strong>The trial bar says to connect to the internet</strong>: Ravenburst hasn't been able to start your trial yet. Connect once and reopen it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Pricing, upgrades and refunds are on the <a href="/pricing">Pricing page</a>.</p>
